## Good example

### Filters are in a consistent order

A clothes shopping website could show which category is selected by keeping the content in the same order but highlighting the selected option. A user moves from 'dresses' to 'tops' and because the navigation order has not changed, they can quickly find and select 'tops' where they expected it to be. This consistency is predictable and reduces the user's effort when using the website.

